8705268358283536":{"a":"<p>Love these old Harry Potter magic wands. They thought to actually make them really work for a penny more than just a plastic stick. Very cool. There are some interesting mobile apps that can use them. Easy to build embedded devices using magnetic sensors. t.co</p>\n<p><a href=\"1718705268358283536-BH-xxEL5hxPGnySM.mp4\">video</a></p>","m":"<h1>Post 1718705268358283536</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1718705268358283536\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2023-10-29T19:04:02Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1718757765043114272":{"a":"<p>@igor_os777 Yes but I&#x27;m using RADARScope and kinda half way know what I&#x27;m looking at. I&#x27;m with you on all the commercial weather apps being broken. You know, I find it odd they all stopped being accurate after most were bought by a certain company who charges extra for accurate weather.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/igor_os777/status/1718743099436867726\">https://x.com/igor_os777/status/1718743099436867726</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1718757765043114272</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1718757765043114272\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2023-10-29T22:32:38Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1718758355253022900":{"a":"<p>@igor_os777 I spent a really lot of my time in the 90s working on software that fed weather stations into the NOAA mesonet computer and it was precisely to avoid this situation. It frustrates my beyond pale the government sold weather out to idiots.</p>","m":"<h1>Post 1718758355253022900</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1718758355253022900\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2023-10-29T22:34:59Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>r